A Single Page Application (SPA) is a web application where the browser loads one main HTML page and the content changes dynamically without completely reloading the page.

React is commonly used to build SPAs.

For example:

Home
AboutSingle Page Application (SPA)
Contact

In a traditional website, clicking each page may reload a new HTML page.

In a React SPA:

Browser
   ↓
React Application
   ↓
Home → About → Contact

The page can change without a full browser refresh.

For multiple pages, React applications commonly use React Router.

Simple Practice Project in VS Code

You can create a simple project demonstrating these concepts.

src/App.jsx
import { useState } from "react";

function App() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

  return (
    <div>
      <h1>My React Application</h1>

      <h2>Introduction to React</h2>

      <p>React is a JavaScript library for building user interfaces.</p>

      <h2>Counter Example</h2>

      <p>Count: {count}</p>

      <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>
        Increase
      </button>
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
